---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import LegalPage from '../components/LegalPage.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="Service Policy — Lakmuthu Studio"
	description="Lakmuthu Studio policies for project inquiries, pricing, scope, payments, revisions, ownership, handover, and post-launch support."
>
	<LegalPage title="Service Policy" updated="28 July 2026">
		<p>Lakmuthu Studio is the independent software service practice of Kaveen Lakmuthu.</p>
		<p>This Service Policy explains how project inquiries, quotes, development work, payments, revisions, handover, and support are handled.</p>

		<h2>Project Inquiries</h2>
		<p>Submitting an inquiry does not create a project agreement. A project begins only after the project scope, price, timeline, payment terms, and starting requirements are agreed in writing.</p>

		<h2>Quotes and Starting Prices</h2>
		<p>Prices shown on the website are starting prices for small, clearly defined projects.</p>
		<p>Final pricing depends on scope, number of pages or screens, backend functionality, database requirements, integrations, deployment needs, platform support, urgency, and support requirements.</p>
		<p>Sri Lankan clients may request LKR quotations after discussing the project scope.</p>

		<h2>Scope Approval</h2>
		<p>Before development begins, I prepare a written scope, feature list, screen outline, UI direction, or proposal depending on the project.</p>
		<p>Development starts only after the client approves the scope and the agreed advance payment is received.</p>

		<h2>Payments</h2>
		<p>Payment terms are agreed before work begins.</p>
		<p>For most projects, payment is handled as:</p>
		<ul>
			<li>advance payment before development starts;</li>
			<li>final payment before final deployment, source code transfer, or full handover.</li>
		</ul>
		<p>Larger projects may be split into milestones.</p>

		<h2>Revisions and Changes</h2>
		<p>Agreed revisions within the approved project scope are included.</p>
		<p>The following may require additional cost and extra time:</p>
		<ul>
			<li>new features;</li>
			<li>new pages or screens;</li>
			<li>major design changes;</li>
			<li>changed workflows;</li>
			<li>backend changes;</li>
			<li>third-party integrations;</li>
			<li>changes requested after scope approval;</li>
			<li>work not included in the original proposal.</li>
		</ul>
		<p>Fixed-price projects require fixed scope.</p>

		<h2>Client Responsibilities</h2>
		<p>The client is responsible for providing required content, images, business details, account access, feedback, approvals, and third-party service information on time.</p>
		<p>Project timelines may change if required client materials, access, approvals, or feedback are delayed.</p>

		<h2>External Costs</h2>
		<p>Development pricing does not include external costs unless clearly stated in the proposal.</p>
		<p>External costs may include:</p>
		<ul>
			<li>domain names;</li>
			<li>hosting;</li>
			<li>email services;</li>
			<li>SMS services;</li>
			<li>payment gateway fees;</li>
			<li>third-party APIs;</li>
			<li>app store fees;</li>
			<li>premium fonts, icons, images, or assets;</li>
			<li>third-party software subscriptions.</li>
		</ul>

		<h2>Source Code and Ownership</h2>
		<p>Source code, project files, deployment details, and handover materials are transferred after final payment, unless otherwise agreed in writing.</p>
		<p>Until final payment is received, project files, source code, and deployment ownership remain under my control.</p>

		<h2>Handover</h2>
		<p>Depending on the project, handover may include:</p>
		<ul>
			<li>source code repository or source archive;</li>
			<li>setup instructions;</li>
			<li>development and build commands;</li>
			<li>deployment notes;</li>
			<li>environment variable list;</li>
			<li>database notes;</li>
			<li>hosting and domain notes;</li>
			<li>admin account instructions;</li>
			<li>third-party service list;</li>
			<li>known limitations;</li>
			<li>support period end date.</li>
		</ul>

		<h2>Post-Launch Support</h2>
		<p>30 days of post-launch bug-fix support is included for issues related to the agreed project scope.</p>
		<p>Included bug support does not cover:</p>
		<ul>
			<li>new features;</li>
			<li>new screens;</li>
			<li>design changes;</li>
			<li>content updates beyond the agreed scope;</li>
			<li>third-party service outages;</li>
			<li>hosting provider issues;</li>
			<li>payment gateway, email, SMS, or API provider issues;</li>
			<li>issues caused by client-side modifications;</li>
			<li>changes made by another developer;</li>
			<li>long-term maintenance.</li>
		</ul>

		<h2>Long-Term Maintenance</h2>
		<p>Long-term maintenance is not included by default.</p>
		<p>If short transition support is needed after launch, it must be discussed before handover.</p>

		<h2>Existing Projects</h2>
		<p>For existing websites, apps, or codebases, I may need to review the project before accepting work. I may decline projects where the codebase, access, security, documentation, or scope is unsuitable.</p>

		<h2>No Guarantee of Results</h2>
		<p>I aim to build reliable, practical, and maintainable software according to the agreed scope.</p>
		<p>However, I do not guarantee specific business results such as sales, traffic, search ranking, conversion rate, app store approval, or revenue unless explicitly agreed in writing.</p>

